.build/
/vibecheck
# The SwiftPM resource bundle `just build-vibecheck-plugin` copies next to
# the binary. Build output, same as the binary — the source of truth is
# Sources/vibecheck/ui/.
/vibecheck_vibecheck.bundle/
# codesign treats this directory as a bundle root once the binary and its
# resource bundle sit here side by side, so re-signing the copied binary
# (needed — see below) writes a resource manifest here. Build output.
#
# `just build-plugins` copies .build/release/vibecheck into this directory,
# and the copy lands with a signature that no longer verifies here:
#   "code has no resources but signature indicates they must be present"
# AMFI then SIGKILLs it on spawn, and core reports `signal: killed`. The
# same binary copied into an otherwise-empty directory verifies fine, which
# is why ~/.vibecare/plugins-v2/vibecheck works. Until the recipe stages
# into a clean directory, `codesign -f -s - plugins/vibecheck/vibecheck`
# after a build makes `just run` work.
/_CodeSignature/
